1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:05,428
Here are the five achievements from our timed woodland run,
together with the Ultimate Achievement trophy.

2
00:00:05,461 --> 00:00:10,023
This is the game's own Achievement Obtained page after a private
test. We'll configure those

3
00:00:10,048 --> 00:00:15,045
goals and connect their progress to the Start, pickup and victory
events we've already built.

4
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:24,674
We'll find the Achievement settings, make five ordinary goals,

5
00:00:24,836 --> 00:00:29,240
configure the Ultimate Achievement, and update progress from
native node graphs.

6
00:00:29,316 --> 00:00:32,685
Then we'll complete the challenge and inspect the actual result
page.

7
00:00:32,835 --> 00:00:37,638
Continue in a separate copy of the working two-minute lesson,
keeping that earlier version available.

8
00:00:38,428 --> 00:00:42,930
Open the System Menu, choose Manage Peripheral System, and open
Achievement.

9
00:00:43,018 --> 00:00:46,696
This module defines the achievements a player can earn in the
stage.

10
00:00:46,858 --> 00:00:51,902
The name, target count and description explain a goal; the graph
supplies its progress.

11
00:00:52,064 --> 00:00:57,780
Naming an achievement First Coin doesn't automatically detect a
pickup. We'll connect that event ourselves.

12
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:04,106
Turn on Enable Achievements and save. For this recording, Test
Play Settlement is enabled,

13
00:01:04,131 --> 00:01:08,649
while in-room achievement settlement remains off. The in-room
option controls progress

14
00:01:08,768 --> 00:01:13,726
for room-team play rather than matchmaking. Our result check uses
private Test Play.

15
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:17,358
Review the setting that matches how you intend players to enter
your own stage.

16
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:24,443
An ordinary achievement has an ID, a rarity, an Achievement Count,
a name and a description.

17
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:29,380
Its progress starts from zero, and reaching the configured count
completes the goal.

18
00:01:29,529 --> 00:01:32,952
We'll use the existing ordinary entry and add four more.

19
00:01:33,113 --> 00:01:36,768
The native rarity supplies the regular medal appearance in this
client.

20
00:01:37,399 --> 00:01:43,970
Edit the first ordinary entry. Name it FreshStart, set Achievement
Count to one, and use Start a timed run

21
00:01:43,996 --> 00:01:49,743
as its description. The current input accepts ten characters for
the name, so read the saved text back.

22
00:01:49,798 --> 00:01:56,145
Our entry has ID two. Your own IDs can differ; write down the ones
actually assigned in your save.

23
00:02:02,513 --> 00:02:08,376
Add First Coin with a target of one, ThreeCoins with a target of
three, and All Five with a target

24
00:02:08,401 --> 00:02:14,660
of five. Their descriptions are Collect one coin, Collect three
coins, and Collect five coins.

25
00:02:14,713 --> 00:02:18,754
Read each name, target and ID back before closing its editor.

26
00:02:18,894 --> 00:02:22,521
These are three milestones driven by the same tested Player
counter.

27
00:02:38,471 --> 00:02:42,609
Add Clear Run with a target of one and the description Win the
timed run.

28
00:02:42,719 --> 00:02:47,208
This is separate from All Five. Collecting the coins finishes the
pickup milestone,

29
00:02:47,241 --> 00:02:51,069
while Clear Run waits for the natural victory path at the end of
the countdown.

30
00:02:51,209 --> 00:02:55,462
Our five ordinary IDs are two through six, but use your own
readback.

31
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:08,814
Edit the Ultimate Achievement. We name it Woodland and choose a
local square JPG trophy for its icon.

32
00:03:09,018 --> 00:03:14,412
The icon supplied with the lesson is adapted from the MIT-licensed
Bootstrap Icons collection.

33
00:03:14,581 --> 00:03:20,136
Only this Ultimate icon is custom-uploaded here; the regular
achievements keep their native medals.

34
00:03:20,341 --> 00:03:23,360
The file chooser is outside the lesson's captured views.

35
00:03:24,094 --> 00:03:27,440
The official guide requires at least five ordinary achievements
for

36
00:03:27,465 --> 00:03:31,016
the Ultimate Achievement, with their names and images configured.

37
00:03:31,092 --> 00:03:36,400
After our five entries and trophy are saved, the Currently not
active warning disappears.

38
00:03:36,569 --> 00:03:41,058
The panel explains that completing all achievements unlocks the
Ultimate Achievement.

39
00:03:41,091 --> 00:03:45,245
This shows a valid configuration. We'll still need to complete the
goals in play.

40
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:49,590
In the node library, choose Set Achievement Progress Tally.

41
00:03:49,696 --> 00:03:54,228
It takes the affected entity, an Achievement ID, and the tally to
set.

42
00:03:54,347 --> 00:03:58,850
We'll target the Player who owns this progress. This is an
absolute value.

43
00:03:59,024 --> 00:04:03,471
If the Player has collected three coins, we set the coin
milestones to three;

44
00:04:03,504 --> 00:04:06,202
we don't increase them by the running total each time.

45
00:04:06,989 --> 00:04:11,999
Open the Player's Round Controller. Insert the achievement action
in the accepted Start chain,

46
00:04:12,024 --> 00:04:18,056
after its existing guards. Target Self, use the ID for FreshStart,
and set the tally to one.

47
00:04:18,081 --> 00:04:20,821
Connect the white execution line through the new node.

48
00:04:20,897 --> 00:04:25,016
An ignored second start request should not become a separate route
around our guard.

49
00:04:32,918 --> 00:04:38,635
Open the coin graph. After writing the new Coins total, use a
separate Get Custom Variable to

50
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:43,612
read that Player's current Coins. We already used this readback
pattern for the printed counter.

51
00:04:43,767 --> 00:04:49,409
Keep the affiliated Player as the target; the disappearing coin
isn't the owner of the Player's achievements.

52
00:04:56,989 --> 00:05:01,486
Continue the execution chain through three Set Achievement
Progress Tally nodes.

53
00:05:01,655 --> 00:05:08,448
Use the IDs for First Coin, ThreeCoins and All Five. Feed the
fresh Coins value into each tally.

54
00:05:08,567 --> 00:05:14,685
Their configured targets are different, so the same count reaches
the milestones at one, three and five.

55
00:05:14,811 --> 00:05:18,523
Keep the existing print and destruction steps connected after the
updates.

56
00:05:29,904 --> 00:05:32,452
Return to the Player controller's victory branch.

57
00:05:32,678 --> 00:05:37,498
After the winning condition is accepted, set the Clear Run
achievement tally to one for Self.

58
00:05:37,606 --> 00:05:42,031
Put this action before Settle Stage. Leave the failure path
without this award.

59
00:05:42,128 --> 00:05:46,724
The Ultimate Achievement is unlocked by the achievement system
when all ordinary goals are complete;

60
00:05:46,864 --> 00:05:49,383
we don't directly grant its ID in our graph.

61
00:05:59,982 --> 00:06:03,874
The official guide says achievement progress can carry across
playthroughs.

62
00:06:03,907 --> 00:06:07,765
Our standard Coins variable starts again for a new challenge
instance,

63
00:06:07,790 --> 00:06:12,593
while achievements describe the player's milestones. This lesson
sets absolute progress

64
00:06:12,712 --> 00:06:17,521
from the current run, and all five goals can be completed in one
winning attempt.

65
00:06:17,747 --> 00:06:22,338
Decide deliberately how progress should behave if you later design
an accumulating goal.

66
00:06:23,029 --> 00:06:27,625
Save both edited graphs, check their mounted names, and Quick Save
the scene.

67
00:06:27,722 --> 00:06:33,299
Read the new execution connections once more. FreshStart belongs
to the accepted Start path.

68
00:06:33,397 --> 00:06:36,407
The three coin milestones follow the stored Player count.

69
00:06:36,498 --> 00:06:42,561
Clear Run belongs to natural victory, before settlement. Each uses
its own ordinary ID.

70
00:06:43,356 --> 00:06:47,717
Start a fresh private test, press F, and collect the five coins.

71
00:06:47,879 --> 00:06:51,557
Watch the same progress bar and countdown from the previous
lessons.

72
00:06:51,676 --> 00:06:56,934
Let the full two minutes expire naturally. The original recording
retains the entire run;

73
00:06:57,010 --> 00:07:02,429
the tutorial removes part of the wait. A full bar alone isn't our
final achievement check.

74
00:07:05,270 --> 00:07:09,580
After Victory, look through the native settlement pages. In our
test,

75
00:07:09,605 --> 00:07:16,206
Achievement Obtained shows FreshStart, First Coin, ThreeCoins, All
Five and Clear Run.

76
00:07:16,388 --> 00:07:20,098
It also shows Unlock an Ultimate Achievement with the trophy we
selected.

77
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:24,978
Read this page as well as the Coins score, so you know which part
of the system actually completed.

78
00:07:25,699 --> 00:07:30,052
This is the result from this private Test Play, with Test Play
Settlement enabled.

79
00:07:30,163 --> 00:07:35,556
It isn't a public-release or permanent-account award check. The
craftsperson level visible on

80
00:07:35,581 --> 00:07:40,734
this account is also separate from our five-achievement
configuration. Check current eligibility

81
00:07:40,759 --> 00:07:45,405
and publishing requirements in the creator interface when
preparing your own stage for release.

82
00:07:46,318 --> 00:07:52,035
Check the ordinary entry's target and actual ID first. Then follow
the event's execution line to

83
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:57,595
the progress node, check its Player target and tally, and inspect
the appropriate settlement page.

84
00:07:57,777 --> 00:08:02,488
For a missing Ultimate Achievement, review all ordinary goals and
its configuration.

85
00:08:02,656 --> 00:08:06,492
Changing a display name won't repair a wrong numeric ID in the
graph.

86
00:08:07,308 --> 00:08:12,872
Try naming the three event types behind these five goals: accepted
Start, a stored coin count,

87
00:08:12,897 --> 00:08:18,049
and natural victory. Explain why All Five and Clear Run can be
separate achievements.

88
00:08:18,168 --> 00:08:22,922
Keep this tested lesson copy. Next we'll deliberately introduce a
small display

89
00:08:22,947 --> 00:08:27,755
fault in another practice copy, diagnose it, and check a
recoverable final build.
